  "title": "Counting maps to nilpotent-by-cyclic groups sees only the ideal of nonzero characters, and inert layers transfer hardness",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "On closed 3-manifolds without F_p-homology, every map over a sector of order d lands in the subgroup generated by the nonzero-character part, so trivial-character generators drop out and the earlier cross-layer example is explained. Hardness passes from any quotient with a pinned surgery construction whose knots avoid the kernel's characters, which decides 153 of 329 residual census algebras.",
